From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] package the CharLS and pyjpegls licences in the built wheel

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; every pyjpegls wheel on PyPI has the same gap, so it needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

setup.py compiles lib/charls/src/*.cpp (CharLS, vendored by the
team-charls/charls submodule pinned at v2.4.2) straight into the
_CharLS extension, so every wheel redistributes CharLS in binary form.
Its BSD-3-Clause licence requires the copyright notice to travel with
the binary, but the repository's only licence text is license.txt
(lowercase), which carries pyjpegls's own MIT text and nothing for
CharLS.

Worse, setuptools' default license-files auto-discovery glob
(LICENSE*/LICENCE*/COPYING*/NOTICE*/AUTHORS*) is case-sensitive on
Linux and never matches license.txt, so the built wheel ships no
licence at all, for either project.

Add LICENSE as an uppercase copy of the existing license.txt (MIT,
verbatim) and LICENSE.charls with the vendored copy's licence text
(BSD-3-Clause, verbatim from team-charls/charls's LICENSE.md) at the
project root: setuptools' default glob then picks up both and copies
them into the wheel's dist-info/licenses/, so no pyproject.toml change
is needed.
---
 LICENSE        | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.charls | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 51 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.charls

diff --git a/LICENSE b/LICENSE
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..03de66a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
